---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import BossMetaResults from "../../components/replay-library/BossMetaResults.astro";
import RequiredHeroIcons from "../../components/campaign/RequiredHeroIcons.astro";
import { graphics } from "../../data/graphics";

const title = "Guild Raid Boss Meta Guide";
const description =
  "Meta and alternate Guild Raid boss teams, built from researched replay data and creator examples.";

const imageSrc = "/images/boss-meta.png";
const webImageSrc = "/images/web/boss-meta.webp";
const imageAlt = "Guild Raid Boss Meta Infographic";

const archiveGuide = {
  title: "Guild Raid Archive",
  href: "/guild-raid/archive",
  description: "Browse previous Guild Raid seasons, boss lineups, maps, and infographic archives.",
  thumbnail: "/images/web/guild-raid-s101-mythic.webp"
};

const relatedGuides = [
  archiveGuide,
  ...graphics.filter(
    (g) =>
      g.href !== Astro.url.pathname &&
      g.href !== "/guild-raid/archive"
  )
];
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Terminus Maximus Infographics`}
  description={description}
  image={webImageSrc}
>
  <Header />

  <main>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>{title}</h1>
    <p>{description}</p>
    <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: July 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section class="infographic-section">
    <h2>Featured Infographic</h2>

    <a
      href={imageSrc}
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      class="image-link"
      data-ga4-infographic-open
      data-ga4-infographic-title={title}
      data-ga4-link-source="image"
    >
      <img
        src={webImageSrc || imageSrc}
        alt={imageAlt}
        class="infographic"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </a>

    <p class="caption">
      <a
        href={imageSrc}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="caption-link"
        data-ga4-infographic-open
        data-ga4-infographic-title={title}
        data-ga4-link-source="caption"
      >
        CLICK FULL-SIZE INFOGRAPHIC
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Boss Meta Guide Basics</h2>
    <div class="markdown-content">
      <div class="markdown-content">
  <p>
    Guild Raid teams are expensive to build, so choosing the right investments matters. This guide identifies the strongest Meta and Alternate teams for every Guild Raid boss using large-scale replay analysis rather than opinion alone.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>⭐ Meta Team</strong> — The strongest overall recommendation for that boss.</li>
    <li><strong>🔄 Alternate Team</strong> — A powerful second option, usually built around a different team archetype.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Every recommendation includes the exact five-character lineup, recommended Machine of War, summary performance statistics, and curated replay examples so you can compare strategies before investing resources.
  </p>
</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Boss Meta Teams &amp; Replay Results</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Explore the recommended Meta and Alternate team for each Guild Raid boss, including the selected lineup, analyzed performance, and curated replay examples.
    </p>
    <BossMetaResults />
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" id="methodology">
    <h2>Methodology & Results</h2>
    <div class="markdown-content">
      <div class="markdown-content">
  <h3>How the Analysis Works</h3>

  <p class="methodology-lead">
    Rather than relying on opinion or isolated showcase videos, these recommendations are built from a <a href="/replay-library/">large dataset</a> of Guild Raid replay videos collected from experienced creators across multiple raid seasons.
  </p>

  <p>
    Each replay is reviewed and cataloged with:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Boss</li>
    <li>Difficulty Tier</li>
    <li>Damage Dealt</li>
    <li>Five-Hero Team Composition</li>
    <li>Machine of War</li>
    <li>Upload Date</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="methodology-key-point">
    The objective is not simply to identify the single highest damage replay, but to determine which complete teams consistently perform best in today's Guild Raid environment.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 1: Measuring Replay Quality</h3>
  <p>
    Every replay receives a quality score based primarily on damage dealt. Performance is adjusted for raid difficulty, giving additional credit to successful clears at higher Legendary and Mythic tiers.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 2: Weighting the Current Meta</h3>
  <p>
    Guild Raid strategies evolve over time. More recent replays receive greater influence through a gradual recency weighting, while older successful strategies continue contributing to the overall analysis.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 3: Identifying the Best Teams</h3>
  <p>
    Replays are first grouped into broader team archetypes before identifying the strongest exact team within each archetype.
  </p>

  <p>
    An exact team consists of:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>The five heroes</li>
    <li>The selected Machine of War</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Machine of War is treated as part of the team itself because changing the Machine of War frequently changes both the strategy and overall performance.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 4: Community Confidence</h3>

  <p class="methodology-key-point">
    Popularity still matters—but only as a confidence signal.
  </p>

  <p>
    Teams that repeatedly appear across successful community replays receive a modest frequency bonus, while average performance remains the primary factor in determining the final rankings. This rewards strategies that consistently succeed without allowing replay volume alone to dominate the results.
  </p>

  <p class="methodology-threshold-callout">
    A five-hero and one Machine of War team needs at least 4 qualifying replays to be considered for the final selection.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 5: Selecting the Final Recommendations</h3>

  <p>
    For each boss, the highest-ranked qualifying archetype becomes the <strong>META</strong> recommendation, while the strongest qualifying alternative archetype becomes the <strong>ALTERNATE</strong> recommendation.
  </p>

  <p>
    Within each recommendation, a single exact team is selected consisting of five heroes and one Machine of War.
  </p>

  <p>
    Minimum replay thresholds ensure recommendations are supported by multiple successful examples. If an alternate archetype lacks sufficient replay data, another well-supported team is selected instead.
  </p>

  <h3>Replay Examples</h3>

  <p>
    The replay examples shown above are curated examples of the exact recommended team—not simply similar teams from the same archetype.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every replay displayed matches the recommended:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Five heroes</li>
    <li>Machine of War</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    This allows you to study positioning, deployment order, movement, and execution from successful runs using the exact lineup being recommended.
  </p>

  <p class="methodology-closing">
    These recommendations represent hundreds of hours of replay collection, validation, and analysis. As new replay data becomes available, future updates automatically adapt to reflect the evolving Guild Raid meta.
  </p>
</div>
    </div>
    <p class="methodology-back-to-bosses">
      <a href="#boss-jump-nav">↑ Back to Boss List</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Related Guides</h2>

    <div class="card-grid">
      {relatedGuides.map((graphic, index) => (
        <a
          class={`card related-guide-card ${index === 0 ? "forced-related-card" : ""}`}
          href={graphic.href}
        >
          <div class="card-image-wrap">
            <img
              src={graphic.thumbnail}
              alt={`${graphic.title} preview`}
              class="card-image"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>

          <h3>{graphic.title}</h3>
          {graphic.requiredHeroes?.length ? (
            <RequiredHeroIcons heroes={graphic.requiredHeroes} />
          ) : (
            <p>{graphic.description}</p>
          )}
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
  </main>

  <script>
  const cards = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(".related-guide-card"));
  const forcedCard = document.querySelector(".forced-related-card");
  const randomCards = cards.filter((card) => card !== forcedCard);

  randomCards
    .sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5)
    .forEach((card, index) => {
      card.style.display = index < 2 ? "block" : "none";
    });

  if (forcedCard) {
    forcedCard.style.display = "block";
  }
  </script>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    background-color: #121212;
    color: #f5f5f5;
    font-family: 'Lexend', sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .hero {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .hero p,
  .section-intro {
    color: #cccccc;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .hero p {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.2rem);
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hero .last-updated {
    color: #d4af37;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .infographic-section,
  .content-section {
    background: #1e1e1e;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  section h2 {
    color: #d4af37;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #333;
  }

  .image-link {
    display: block;
  }

  .infographic {
    max-width: 700px;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 8px;
    display: block;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .caption {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .caption-link {
    display: block;
    text-align: center;
    color: #d4af37;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .caption-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .markdown-content {
    color: #cccccc;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  #methodology {
    scroll-margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  #methodology .markdown-content > .markdown-content {
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 980px;
  }

  #methodology .markdown-content h3 {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.12), rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.02));
    border-left: 3px solid #d4af37;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    color: #d4af37;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  }

  #methodology .markdown-content h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  #methodology .markdown-content p {
    margin: 0.8rem 0;
  }

  #methodology .markdown-content a {
    color: #d4af37;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.65);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }

  #methodology .markdown-content a:hover,
  #methodology .markdown-content a:focus-visible {
    color: #f5d76e;
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  #methodology .markdown-content strong {
    color: #f5d76e;
  }

  #methodology .markdown-content ul {
    background: #161616;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    border-radius: 8px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem 1.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: 0.85rem 0 1.1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem 0.85rem 2.4rem;
  }

  #methodology .markdown-content li::marker {
    color: #d4af37;
  }

  #methodology .methodology-lead,
  #methodology .methodology-closing {
    background: #151515;
    border: 1px solid #3a3a3a;
    border-left: 3px solid #d4af37;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #e4e4e4;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
  }

  #methodology .methodology-lead {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }

  #methodology .methodology-key-point {
    border-left: 2px solid rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.65);
    color: #e0e0e0;
    font-weight: 650;
    padding: 0.2rem 0 0.2rem 0.9rem;
  }

  #methodology .methodology-threshold-callout {
    align-items: flex-start;
    background: #161616;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    border-left: 3px solid #d4af37;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #e4e4e4;
    display: flex;
    font-weight: 400;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    margin: 0.85rem 0 1.1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
  }

  #methodology .methodology-threshold-callout::before {
    color: #d4af37;
    content: "•";
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  #methodology .methodology-closing {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .methodology-back-to-bosses {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .methodology-back-to-bosses a {
    background: #121212;
    border: 1px solid #444;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: #d4af37;
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.85rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .methodology-back-to-bosses a:hover,
  .methodology-back-to-bosses a:focus-visible {
    border-color: #d4af37;
    outline: none;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 320px));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    justify-content: start;
  }

  .card {
    background: #121212;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .card:hover,
  .card:focus-visible {
    border-color: #d4af37;
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    outline: none;
  }

  .card-image-wrap {
    width: 100%;
    height: 120px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    background: #121212;
    border: 1px solid #333;
  }

  .card-image {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    object-position: top;
    display: block;
  }

  .card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: #d4af37;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .card p {
    color: #cccccc;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    main {
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .hero {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    section {
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }

    .infographic-section,
    .content-section {
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .card-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .card {
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    #methodology .markdown-content ul {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

    html {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

</style>
